#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install Qiskit {#install-qiskit}"
msgstr "I-install ang Qiskit {#install-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Whether you will work locally or in a cloud environment, the first step for "
"all users is to install Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lokal ka man magtrabaho o sa cloud environment, ang unang hakbang para sa "
"lahat ng mga user ay ang pag-install ng Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Upgrade from Qiskit 0.x to Qiskit 1.0 and beyond\">\n"
"  (If you are installing Qiskit for the first time, skip ahead to the [Install and set up](#local) section. This notice is relevant only to users who have installed Qiskit previously.)\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Pag-upgrade mula sa Qiskit 0.x patungong Qiskit 1.0 at mas bago\">\n"
"  (Kung ito ang unang beses mong mag-i-install ng Qiskit, dumiretso ka na sa seksyong [I-install at i-set up](#local). Ang abisong ito ay para lamang sa mga user na nakaraang nag-install ng Qiskit.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  **For those upgrading from version 0.x to 1.0 or later**: note that "
"because Qiskit v1.0 uses a new packaging structure, you **cannot** use `pip "
"install -U qiskit` to upgrade from any Qiskit 0.x version to 1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"  **Para sa mga nag-a-upgrade mula sa bersyon 0.x patungong 1.0 o mas "
"bago**: tandaan na dahil gumagamit ang Qiskit v1.0 ng bagong packaging "
"structure, **hindi** mo magagamit ang `pip install -U qiskit` para mag-"
"upgrade mula sa anumang Qiskit 0.x na bersyon patungong 1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  See the [Qiskit 1.0 migration guide](/guides/qiskit-1.0) for details and "
"instructions.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Tingnan ang [Qiskit 1.0 migration guide](/guides/qiskit-1.0) para sa mga "
"detalye at tagubilin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Future updates starting with Qiskit 1.0 will allow for in-place upgrades.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Ang mga susunod na update simula sa Qiskit 1.0 ay magbibigay-daan sa in-place na mga upgrade.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"local\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"local\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Qiskit SDK {#install-the-qiskit-sdk}"
msgstr "I-install ang Qiskit SDK {#install-the-qiskit-sdk}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install Python. Check the \"Programming Language\" section on the [Qiskit "
"PyPI project page](https://pypi.org/project/qiskit/) to determine which "
"Python versions are supported by the most recent release. For download "
"instructions, see the [Python Beginners "
"Guide](https://wiki.python.org/moin/BeginnersGuide/Download).\n"
msgstr ""
"Mag-install ng Python. Tingnan ang seksyong \"Programming Language\" sa "
"[Qiskit PyPI project page](https://pypi.org/project/qiskit/) para malaman "
"kung aling mga bersyon ng Python ang sinusuportahan ng pinakabagong release."
" Para sa mga tagubilin sa pag-download, tingnan ang [Python Beginners "
"Guide](https://wiki.python.org/moin/BeginnersGuide/Download).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    It is recommended that you use [Python virtual "
"environments](https://docs.python.org/3.10/tutorial/venv.html) to separate "
"Qiskit from other applications.\n"
msgstr ""
"    Inirerekomenda na gumamit ka ng [Python virtual "
"environments](https://docs.python.org/3.10/tutorial/venv.html) para ihiwalay"
" ang Qiskit mula sa ibang mga application.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"    These instructions use the standard Python distribution from [pypi.org](https://pypi.org/). However, you can use other Python distributions, such as [Anaconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/anaconda/) or [miniconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/miniconda/), along with other dependency management workflows like [Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/docs/).\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"    <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"    Gumagamit ang mga tagubiling ito ng standard na Python distribution mula sa [pypi.org](https://pypi.org/). Gayunpaman, maaari kang gumamit ng ibang mga Python distribution, tulad ng [Anaconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/anaconda/) o [miniconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/miniconda/), kasama ang ibang mga dependency management workflow tulad ng [Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/docs/).\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"If you're new to virtual environments, click to expand for more information.\">\n"
"    A virtual Python environment is an isolated space to work with Python for a specific purpose — so you can install whatever packages you wish, and set up libraries, dependencies, and so on, without affecting the \"base\" Python environment on your machine.\n"
msgstr ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"If you're new to virtual environments, click to expand for more information.\">\n"
"    Ang isang virtual Python environment ay isang isolated na espasyo para magtrabaho kasama ang Python para sa isang tiyak na layunin — kaya maaari kang mag-install ng kahit anong mga pakete, at mag-set up ng mga library, dependency, at iba pa, nang hindi naaapektuhan ang \"base\" na Python environment sa iyong makina.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    One important advantage of a virtual environment is that if your Python "
"environment becomes corrupted somewhere along the way, you can easily delete"
" the virtual environment and start over!\n"
msgstr ""
"    Isang mahalagang kalamangan ng virtual environment ay kung masira ang "
"iyong Python environment sa kalagitnaan ng trabaho mo, madali mo itong ma-"
"delete at magsimula ulit!\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Choose a preferred location in which to store information about your virtual environments. Typically they're stored in a directory named `.venv` within each project directory you're working in.\n"
"    </AccordionItem>\n"
"    </Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"    Pumili ng gustong lokasyon kung saan iiimbak ang impormasyon tungkol sa iyong mga virtual environment. Kadalasan, ini-imbak ang mga ito sa isang direktoryo na pinangalanang `.venv` sa loob ng bawat project directory na pinagtatrabahuhan mo.\n"
"    </AccordionItem>\n"
"    </Accordion>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    First, navigate to your project directory and create a minimal "
"environment with only Python installed in it.\n"
msgstr ""
"    Una, pumunta sa iyong project directory at gumawa ng minimal na "
"environment na may Python lamang na naka-install dito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```shell\n"
"            python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"            ```shell\n"
"            python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"
msgstr "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
msgstr "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```text\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"            ```text\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "    Next, activate your new environment.\n"
msgstr "    Susunod, i-activate ang iyong bagong environment.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"         <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"           <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"
msgstr ""
"         <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"           <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```shell\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```shell\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "           <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"
msgstr "           <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"           <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
"              If using PowerShell:\n"
msgstr ""
"           <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
"              Kung gumagamit ng PowerShell:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\n"
"             ```\n"
"             If using Git Bash:\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\n"
"             ```\n"
"             Kung gumagamit ng Git Bash:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```text\n"
"             source .venv/scripts/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"              If using command prompt:\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```text\n"
"             source .venv/scripts/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"              Kung gumagamit ng command prompt:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Install pip](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/installation/) if it's not "
"already installed in your environment. Pip is a Python package manager that "
"you use to install Qiskit and other Python packages. Use `pip list` to see "
"what is in your virtual environment. In most Python environments, pip is "
"already installed.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Mag-install ng pip](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/installation/) kung hindi"
" pa ito naka-install sa iyong environment. Ang pip ay isang Python package "
"manager na ginagamit mo para mag-install ng Qiskit at ibang mga Python "
"package. Gamitin ang `pip list` para makita kung ano ang nasa iyong virtual "
"environment. Sa karamihan ng mga Python environment, naka-install na ang "
"pip.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Qiskit SDK.\n"
msgstr "I-install ang Qiskit SDK.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      pip install qiskit\n"
"      ```\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      pip install qiskit\n"
"      ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      <Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Add visualization support\">\n"
"      If you intend to use visualization functionality or Jupyter notebooks, also install the `qiskit.visualization` module. See the [Visualizations API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/visualization) for more information.\n"
"      </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"      <Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Magdagdag ng suporta sa visualization\">\n"
"      Kung balak mong gumamit ng visualization functionality o Jupyter notebooks, i-install din ang `qiskit.visualization` module. Tingnan ang [Visualizations API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/visualization) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"
"      </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<span id=\"local-jupyter\"></span>\n"
"1. If you want to run a Jupyter notebook with the Qiskit packages you just installed, you need to install Jupyter in your environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"<span id=\"local-jupyter\"></span>\n"
"1. Kung gusto mong magpatakbo ng Jupyter notebook kasama ang mga Qiskit package na na-install mo lang, kailangan mong mag-install ng Jupyter sa iyong environment.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      pip install jupyter\n"
"      ```\n"
"    Then open your notebook as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      pip install jupyter\n"
"      ```\n"
"    Pagkatapos, buksan ang iyong notebook tulad nito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      jupyter notebook <path/to/notebook.ipynb>\n"
"      ```\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      jupyter notebook <path/to/notebook.ipynb>\n"
"      ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are planning to work locally and use simulators built into Qiskit, "
"then your installation is done. If you want to run jobs on IBM&reg; QPUs, "
"continue on to [set up your IBM Cloud&reg; account](cloud-setup).\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung plano kang magtrabaho nang lokal at gumamit ng mga simulator na built "
"into Qiskit, tapos na ang iyong pag-install. Kung gusto mong magpatakbo ng "
"mga job sa IBM&reg; QPUs, magpatuloy sa [pag-set up ng iyong IBM Cloud&reg; "
"account](cloud-setup).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Stay current with the latest versions\">\n"
"Periodically check the [Qiskit release notes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/release-notes) to see new releases. We recommend frequently updating your requirements for `qiskit` by running `pip install -U qiskit`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Manatiling updated sa pinakabagong mga bersyon\">\n"
"Pana-panahon, tingnan ang [Qiskit release notes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/release-notes) para makita ang mga bagong release. Inirerekomenda namin na madalas mong i-update ang iyong mga requirement para sa `qiskit` sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatakbo ng `pip install -U qiskit`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting {#troubleshooting}"
msgstr "Pag-troubleshoot {#troubleshooting}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`No Module 'qiskit'` error with Jupyter Notebook\">\n"
"  If you used ``pip install qiskit`` and set up your virtual environment in\n"
"  Anaconda, then you may get the ``No Module 'qiskit'`` error when you run a tutorial\n"
"  in Jupyter Notebook. If you have not installed Qiskit or set up your\n"
"  virtual environment, you can follow the [installation](#qiskit-install) steps.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`No Module 'qiskit'` error with Jupyter Notebook\">\n"
"  Kung ginamit mo ang ``pip install qiskit`` at nag-set up ng iyong virtual environment sa\n"
"  Anaconda, maaari kang makakuha ng error na ``No Module 'qiskit'`` kapag nagpatakbo ka ng tutorial\n"
"  sa Jupyter Notebook. Kung hindi pa naka-install ang Qiskit o hindi pa na-set up ang iyong\n"
"  virtual environment, maaari mong sundin ang mga hakbang sa [pag-install](#qiskit-install).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The error is caused when trying to import the Qiskit package in an\n"
"  environment where Qiskit is not installed. If you launched Jupyter Notebook\n"
"  from the Anaconda-Navigator, it is possible that Jupyter Notebook is running\n"
"  in the base (root) environment, instead of in your virtual\n"
"  environment. Choose a virtual environment in the Anaconda-Navigator from the\n"
"  **Applications on** dropdown menu. In this menu, you can see\n"
"  all of the virtual environments within Anaconda, and you can\n"
"  select the environment where you have Qiskit installed to launch Jupyter\n"
"  Notebook.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Ang error ay sanhi ng pagsubok na mag-import ng Qiskit package sa isang\n"
"  environment kung saan hindi naka-install ang Qiskit. Kung inilunsad mo ang Jupyter Notebook\n"
"  mula sa Anaconda-Navigator, posible na tumatakbo ang Jupyter Notebook\n"
"  sa base (root) environment, sa halip na sa iyong virtual\n"
"  environment. Pumili ng virtual environment sa Anaconda-Navigator mula sa\n"
"  dropdown menu na **Applications on**. Sa menu na ito, makikita mo\n"
"  ang lahat ng virtual environment sa loob ng Anaconda, at maaari kang\n"
"  pumili ng environment kung saan naka-install ang Qiskit para ilunsad ang Jupyter\n"
"  Notebook.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Compilation errors during installation\">\n"
"  Qiskit depends on a number of other open-source Python packages, which\n"
"  are automatically installed when doing ``pip install qiskit``. Depending on\n"
"  your system's platform and Python version, it is possible that a particular\n"
"  package does not provide pre-built binaries for your system. You can refer\n"
"  to [Operating system support](#operating-system-support) for a list of platforms supported by Qiskit, some\n"
"  of which may need an extra compiler. In cases where there are\n"
"  no precompiled binaries available, ``pip`` will attempt to compile the package\n"
"  from source, which in turn might require some extra dependencies that need to\n"
"  be installed manually.\n"
msgstr ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Compilation errors during installation\">\n"
"  Nakadepende ang Qiskit sa ilang ibang open-source na Python package, na\n"
"  awtomatikong ina-install kapag ginawa ang ``pip install qiskit``. Depende sa\n"
"  platform at bersyon ng Python ng iyong system, posible na ang isang partikular\n"
"  na pakete ay walang pre-built na mga binary para sa iyong system. Maaari kang sumangguni sa\n"
"  [Operating system support](#operating-system-support) para sa listahan ng mga platform na sinusuportahan ng Qiskit, na ilan sa mga ito\n"
"  ay maaaring mangailangan ng karagdagang compiler. Sa mga kaso kung saan walang\n"
"  available na precompiled na mga binary, susubukan ng ``pip`` na i-compile ang pakete\n"
"  mula sa source, na maaaring mangailangan naman ng ilang karagdagang dependency na kailangang\n"
"  i-install nang manu-mano.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  If the output of ``pip install qiskit`` contains similar lines to:\n"
msgstr ""
"  Kung ang output ng ``pip install qiskit`` ay naglalaman ng mga linya na "
"katulad ng:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  please check the documentation of the package that failed to install (in the\n"
"  example code, ``SOME_PACKAGE``) for information on how to install the libraries\n"
"  needed for compiling from source.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"  pakitingnan ang dokumentasyon ng paketeng nabigo sa pag-install (sa\n"
"  halimbawang code, ``SOME_PACKAGE``) para sa impormasyon kung paano i-install ang mga library\n"
"  na kailangan para sa pag-compile mula sa source.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"os-support\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"os-support\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Operating system support {#operating-system-support}"
msgstr "Suporta sa operating system {#operating-system-support}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit strives to support as many operating systems as possible, but due to "
"limitations in available testing resources and operating system "
"availability, not all operating systems can be supported. Operating system "
"support for Qiskit is broken into three tiers with different levels of "
"support for each tier. For platforms outside these, such as FreeBSD or "
"WebAssembly (WASI), Qiskit may still be installable, but it is not tested "
"and you will have to build Qiskit (and likely Qiskit’s dependencies) from "
"source.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagsisikap ang Qiskit na suportahan ang mas maraming operating system "
"hangga't maaari, ngunit dahil sa mga limitasyon sa available na testing "
"resources at availability ng operating system, hindi lahat ng operating "
"system ay maaaring suportahan. Ang suporta sa operating system para sa "
"Qiskit ay nahahati sa tatlong tier na may iba't ibang antas ng suporta para "
"sa bawat tier. Para sa mga platform na wala sa mga ito, tulad ng FreeBSD o "
"WebAssembly (WASI), maaaring mai-install pa rin ang Qiskit, ngunit hindi ito"
" tinotest at kailangan mong buuin ang Qiskit (at malamang ang mga dependency"
" ng Qiskit) mula sa source.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Additionally, Qiskit only supports the CPython implementation of the Python "
"language. Running with other Python interpreters such as PyPy is not "
"supported.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bukod dito, sinusuportahan lamang ng Qiskit ang CPython na implementasyon ng"
" wikang Python. Hindi sinusuportahan ang pagpapatakbo gamit ang ibang mga "
"Python interpreter tulad ng PyPy.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit v2.x {#qiskit-v2x}"
msgstr "Qiskit v2.x {#qiskit-v2x}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In the Qiskit v2.x release series, the supported platforms are:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa Qiskit v2.x na release series, ang mga sinusuportahang platform ay:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tier 1\">\n"
"  Tier 1 operating systems are fully tested as part of the development processes to ensure any proposed change will function correctly. Pre-compiled binaries are built, tested, and published to PyPI as part of the release process. Typically, as long as there is a functioning Python environment installed, Qiskit can be installed on these operating systems without needing to install further dependencies.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tier 1\">\n"
"  Ang mga Tier 1 na operating system ay ganap na tinotest bilang bahagi ng mga proseso ng development para matiyak na ang anumang iminungkahing pagbabago ay gagana nang tama. Ang mga pre-compiled na binary ay binubuo, tinotest, at nila-publish sa PyPI bilang bahagi ng proseso ng release. Kadalasan, basta't may gumaganang Python environment na naka-install, maaaring i-install ang Qiskit sa mga operating system na ito nang hindi na kailangang mag-install ng karagdagang dependency.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  Tier 1 operating systems:\n"
msgstr "  Mga Tier 1 na operating system:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Linux x86_64 (distributions compatible with the [manylinux "
"2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/) packaging specification).\n"
msgstr ""
"Linux x86_64 (mga distribution na compatible sa [manylinux "
"2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/) packaging specification).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "macOS ARM64 (11.0 or newer)\n"
msgstr "macOS ARM64 (11.0 o mas bago)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Windows 64-bit (Windows 10 and later supported)\n"
msgstr "Windows 64-bit (sinusuportahan ang Windows 10 at mas bago)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  - Linux AArch64 (distributions compatible with the [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/) packaging specification)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tier 2\">\n"
"  Tier 2 operating systems are not tested as part of the development process. However, pre-compiled binaries are built, tested, and published to PyPI as part of the release process, and these packages can be expected to be installed with only a functioning Python environment.\n"
"  There might be a delay in releasing packages for these systems, since test failures might not be detected until much later, and failures during publishing will not block the publication of the package for Tier 1 systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"  - Linux AArch64 (mga distribution na compatible sa [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/) packaging specification)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tier 2\">\n"
"  Ang mga Tier 2 na operating system ay hindi tinotest bilang bahagi ng proseso ng development. Gayunpaman, ang mga pre-compiled na binary ay binubuo, tinotest, at nila-publish sa PyPI bilang bahagi ng proseso ng release, at ang mga paketeng ito ay maaaring i-install nang may gumaganang Python environment lamang.\n"
"  Maaaring magkaroon ng pagkaantala sa pag-release ng mga pakete para sa mga system na ito, dahil ang mga test failure ay maaaring hindi matukoy hanggang sa mas matagal, at ang mga failure sa pag-publish ay hindi hahadlang sa pag-publish ng pakete para sa mga Tier 1 na system.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  Tier 2 operating systems:\n"
msgstr "  Mga Tier 2 na operating system:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  - macOS x86_64 (10.12 or later)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tier 3\">\n"
"  Tier 3 operating systems are not tested as part of the development process. Pre-compiled binaries are built and published to PyPI as part of the release process but are not tested. They may not be installable with only a functioning Python environment and might require a C/C++ compiler or additional programs to build dependencies from source as part of the installation process. Support for these operating systems are best effort only.\n"
msgstr ""
"  - macOS x86_64 (10.12 o mas bago)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tier 3\">\n"
"  Ang mga Tier 3 na operating system ay hindi tinotest bilang bahagi ng proseso ng development. Ang mga pre-compiled na binary ay binubuo at nila-publish sa PyPI bilang bahagi ng proseso ng release ngunit hindi tinotest. Maaaring hindi mai-install ang mga ito nang may gumaganang Python environment lamang at maaaring mangailangan ng C/C++ compiler o karagdagang programa para buuin ang mga dependency mula sa source bilang bahagi ng proseso ng pag-install. Ang suporta para sa mga operating system na ito ay best effort lamang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  Tier 3 operating systems:\n"
msgstr "  Mga Tier 3 na operating system:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Linux ppc64le (distributions compatible with the [manylinux "
"2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/)packaging specification)\n"
msgstr ""
"Linux ppc64le (mga distribution na compatible sa [manylinux "
"2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/)packaging specification)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  - Linux s390x (distributions compatible with the [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/) packaging specification)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"  - Linux s390x (mga distribution na compatible sa [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/) packaging specification)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Starting in Qiskit v2.0.0, only 64-bit platforms are supported and 32-bit platforms are not supported. You will not be able to build from source\n"
"on 32-bit platforms either, as internally the Qiskit Rust code assumes a 64-bit pointer width.\n"
msgstr ""
"Simula sa Qiskit v2.0.0, ang mga 64-bit na platform lamang ang "
"sinusuportahan at hindi sinusuportahan ang mga 32-bit na platform. Hindi ka "
"rin makakabuo mula sa source sa mga 32-bit na platform, dahil ang Qiskit "
"Rust code sa loob ay nag-aasume ng 64-bit na luwang ng pointer.\n"

